#   libcef/browser/chrome/extensions/wubble_ext{.h,.cc,_capi.h,_impl.h}: the
#   plain C table cef_wubble_ext_v1 (set_delegate, set_state, tab_opened,
#   action_click, action_state, free_string, free_action), a UI-thread
#   registry that makes one WindowController per (wubble window, loaded
#   profile) (ported from Chromium's AppWindowController and AppBaseWindow),
#   gives each wubble tab its window id (SessionTabHelper::SetWindowID), and
#   dispatches tabs.onCreated/onRemoved/onActivated (onActivated also for a
#   tab inserted active) and windows.onFocusChanged
#   through TabsEventRouter (as its friend). BUILD.gn lists every file of the
#   module, including those patches 20 and 30 add.
# Why: wubble's tabs are windowless Alloy browsers; Chromium's chrome.tabs and
#   chrome.windows only walk Browser windows and their tab strips, so
#   extensions see no tab and no window (docs/research/extensions.md). A
#   translated CEF API would need regenerated cef-dll-sys bindings; one
#   exported cef_* function looked up at run time keeps stock CEF working.
# Applies in: chromium/src/cef (git apply -p1), after CEF's own patches.
